===Etymology 1===
Attested first from the year 1731, borrowed from {{bor|ru|pl|kozyr}}, also {{m|pl|kozer}}, variants of {{m|pl|kozyra}}, {{m|pl|kozera|t=trump; [[cardsharp|card-sharper]]; card-game; struggle, calamity<!-- later: reason, cause (17<sup>th</sup> century according to Sławski)-->}}, a dialectal variant – already attested in the 16<sup>th</sup> century in the sense “trump”<!--according to Franciszek Sławski--> – of {{m|pl|kostera}}, {{m|pl|kostyra|t=card sharper}}, from {{m|pl|kość|t=die}}, also {{m|pl|kozyrnik}}, {{m|pl|kozernik|t=[[cardshark|card-shark]]; [[fullam]]-player}}.

Compare as another cardgame term that has passed into Russian from Polish: {{m|ru|шу́лер|t=[[cardsharp|card-sharp]]}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA|ко́зырь}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Pacha Tchernof-козырь.wav}}

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+|e|ко́зырь|m|adj=козырно́й,козы́рный}}

# [[trump]]
# {{lb|ru|idiomatic}} main argument, used in the right time to gain advantage
# {{lb|ru|idiomatic}} unrevealed or hidden advantage
#: {{uxi|ru|[[припасти|припасённый]] '''ко́зырь'''|to have cards up one's sleave}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[кто́-то]] припа́с '''ко́зырь''' |someone still has cards up their sleaves; they  haven't played all their cards}}

